{
 "about": "Which of the app's screens goes into which phone of the wiki's paintings (tools/make-wiki-screens.py). screens: where each comes from: a render-test golden in the Games repo (SpeedometerWallpaper/<module>/src/test/screenshots/<file>, module logic_render unless named; crop = the part shown, in px), or a frame of the demo drive that DemoDriveFramesTest renders with the wallpaper's own renderer (<style>/<frame>.jpg, 1080x2400); overlays = Android's status bar and the key art's home screen, laid on after the screen is fitted. entries: each painting's phones: glass = the painted glass's corners (top left, top right, bottom right, bottom left, in the painting's px), the screen, and how it sits: bezel and corner as shares of the glass's short side; stretch = how much the screen may be stretched to the painted display's shape (1.12 = 12 %, more for a phone seen at an angle), past which it is padded with its own edge pixels (fill edge, the default), mirrored (mirror) or a colour; light, camera, blur, spill; keep = where the painting stays on top (a hand, a clamp, the dashboard), with feather in px and test skin for a hand; clean = made-up glyphs outside the screens filled in (a polygon: its bright marks; {poly, all: true}: the whole area, for a label on a plain face); crop = a box the finished picture is cut to and scaled back from (a flat band the painting came with).",
